A.aWd={"Electrical hazards":0,"Natural gas / propane leak hazards":1,"Hazardous chemicals":2,"Radiological / nuclear":3,"Structural / collapse":4,"Biohazard / bloodborne":5}
A.aUU=new B.bZ(A.aWd,["Electrical energy may remain present in damaged wiring, panels, meters, generators, temporary power, or energized equipment after fire or explosion damage. Before invasive exam or destructive opening, confirm utility status with the authority having jurisdiction or utility company when practical. Treat unknown conductors and wet environments as energized until verified otherwise. Document PPE, lockout/tagout or isolation steps actually used, and any areas deferred because power status could not be confirmed.","Fuel-gas leak, residual gas, damaged piping, meters, regulators, or tanks may create asphyxiation, fire, or explosion risk. Confirm gas shutoff / isolation with the gas utility or AHJ when practical before entering or working near suspected leak areas. Do not use open flame or unprotected ignition sources in areas where gas may accumulate. Document odor, meter readings if taken by qualified personnel, ventilation actions, and any zones held pending gas clearance.","Chemicals, residues, pesticides, solvents, cleaners, industrial products, or unknown containers may present inhalation, absorption, reactivity, or contamination hazards. Identify placards, labels, and SDS when available without unnecessary disturbance. Use appropriate respiratory and skin protection for the materials suspected. Document product names or UN/NA numbers only when observed on labels or reported by a reliable source; do not invent chemical identities. Note decontamination and evidence-handling steps that affect chemical exposure.","Radiological or nuclear materials, if identified or reasonably suspected, require specialized monitoring and control beyond ordinary fire-scene PPE. Do not enter controlled radiological areas without qualified radiation-safety support. Document who identified the concern, monitoring used if any, and areas deferred or released only after competent clearance.","Fire, explosion, or suppression may have weakened floors, roofs, walls, stairs, chimneys, or overhead assemblies. Treat unsupported members, hanging debris, and compromised means of egress as collapse hazards. Use structural assessment from qualified personnel when available before deep interior exam. Document shoring, restricted zones, routes used, and areas not entered because of collapse risk.","Blood, body fluids, medical waste, or other potentially infectious materials may be present after injury, fatality, or medical response. Use bloodborne-pathogen precautions (gloves, eye protection, and other PPE as indicated). Avoid unnecessary contact with sharps and contaminated soft goods. Document biohazard areas observed, PPE used, and coordination with medical examiner / law enforcement when applicable. Do not invent that a death or injury occurred unless already recorded elsewhere as a fact on this worksheet."],t.li)
